<item>
            <title>[PBV7-484] Build independently deployable realtime WebSocket platform</title>
                <link>https://propago.atlassian.net/browse/PBV7-484</link>
                <project id="11202" key="PBV7">Propago Backend (V7)</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Objectiveandsource&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Objective and source&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Build an independently deployable .NET 10 Native AOT realtime WebSocket platform using Redis, Kubernetes, Traefik/MetalLB, Helm automation, and provisioned Grafana diagnostics.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Source specification: &lt;a href=&quot;https://propago.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/DK/pages/2592604161/Realtime+WebSocket+Platform+.NET+10+Redis+and+Kubernetes&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noreferrer&quot;&gt;Realtime WebSocket Platform &#8211; .NET 10, Redis, and Kubernetes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Currentstate%2Ftargetstate&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Current state / target state&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The current application requires a scalable realtime capability without depending on SignalR-specific runtime behavior. The target is a standalone, independently versioned gateway with explicit WebSocket contracts, Redis-based horizontal fan-out, optional durable Streams delivery, an SDK-published OCI image, and a separate Helm release.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Technicalscope&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Technical scope&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Standalone .NET 10 solution, projects, test suites, container package, and release pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Native AOT-compatible WebSocket protocol, authentication, authorization, backpressure, reconnect, and graceful draining.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Existing Redis session integration, Pub/Sub fan-out, and optional Streams replay.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes workloads, Helm packaging, PowerShell automation, Traefik WSS routing, and MetalLB exposure.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Metrics, alerts, version-controlled Grafana dashboard, load testing, runbooks, and production-readiness evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Successcriteria&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Success criteria&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;A clean checkout builds, tests, Native AOT-publishes, and produces an independently deployable OCI image.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Two or more gateway replicas exchange events through Redis and support reconnection to a different pod.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Clients connect securely through &lt;tt&gt;realtime.propago.local&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Redis delivery semantics, tenant isolation, backpressure, failure recovery, and graceful rollout behavior are tested.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Helm and PowerShell automation complies with the governing Propago scripting standard.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Grafana dashboard and alerts are provisioned from version-controlled artifacts and identify injected service, Redis, Kubernetes, Traefik, and MetalLB failures.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Measured load and soak tests establish documented capacity and scaling thresholds.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Deployment, rollback, troubleshooting, security, and operations documentation completes technical review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Dependencies&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Dependencies&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes cluster and approved namespace strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Existing Redis session contract and credentials integration.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Approved Redis Helm chart or external Redis endpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Traefik, MetalLB, DNS, certificate, Prometheus-compatible metrics, and Grafana access.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;PropagoLLC/Standards&lt;/tt&gt; repository and current Scripts manifest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Riskmitigation&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Risk mitigation&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Stage all infrastructure and protocol work before production rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Keep gateway pods private behind a ClusterIP Service.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use standards-compliant prerequisite validation, backups, dry-run/diff, bounded waits, validation, rollback, logging, and secret redaction.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Load-test long-lived connections and validate pod, node, Redis, ingress, and VIP failure behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Outofscope&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Out of scope&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Unapproved migration of existing consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Treating Redis Pub/Sub as the business system of record.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Uncontrolled mutation of shared or production infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Unrelated PBV7 feature work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
